-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1,\"repo\":\"sirhc/saml2aws.plugin.zsh\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - Adds completions for <a href=\"https://github.com/Versent/saml2aws\">saml2aws</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Versent/saml2aws\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.4k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1363,\"repo\":\"Versent/saml2aws\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T14:03:52.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"antdimot/awesome-lowcode","categoryHTML":"<h2>Automation</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://camunda.com/\">Camunda</a> - Automate Any Process, Anywhere.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T09:59:40.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/machine-learning\">Recommended course: Prof. Andrew Ng's <em>Machine Learning</em> on Coursera</a></h2><h3>Tips for studying</h3>","itemHTML":"<li>Review tips from <a href=\"https://github.com/ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers#the-daily-plan\">Nam Vu's guide to learning ML as a software engineer</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers#the-daily-plan\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">25.6k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":25556,\"repo\":\"ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2><h4>Towards Expertise</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Ask a question. Start exploring some data.</strong> The <a href=\"https://github.com/DataScienceSpecialization/courses/blob/master/01_DataScientistToolbox/03_02_whatIsData/index.Rmd#the-data-is-the-second-most-important-thing\">\"most important thing in data science is the question\"</a> (<a href=\"https://github.com/jtleek\">Dr. Jeff T. Leek</a>). So start with a question. Then, find <a href=\"https://github.com/caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\">real data</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">46.7k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":46739,\"repo\":\"caesar0301/awesome-public-datasets\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. Analyze it. Then ...</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Risks</h2><h4>Towards Expertise</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><strong>Communicate results.</strong> When you think you have a novel finding, ask for review.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Deep Learning</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://distill.pub/about/\">Distill.pub</a> publishes explorable explanations that are really great.\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://distill.pub/2017/feature-visualization/\">\"Feature Visualization: How neural networks build up their understanding of images\"</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More ways to \"Dive into Machine Learning\"</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Courses by cloud vendors (might be specific to their tools/platforms)\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/\">Machine Learning Crash Course from Google</a> with TensorFlow APIs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/training/learn-about/machine-learning/\">Amazon AWS</a> Amazon have open up their internal training to the public and also offer certification.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More ways to \"Dive into Machine Learning\"</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://xyclade.github.io/MachineLearning/\">Machine Learning for Developers</a> is good for people who are more familiar with Java or Scala than Python.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More ways to \"Dive into Machine Learning\"</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/rasbt/python-machine-learning-book-3rd-edition\">rasbt/python-machine-learning-book-3rd-edition</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/rasbt/python-machine-learning-book-3rd-edition\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">2.9k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":2863,\"repo\":\"rasbt/python-machine-learning-book-3rd-edition\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> aka <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/25545994-python-machine-learning\"><em>Python Machine Learning: Machine Learning and Deep Learning with Python, scikit-learn, and TensorFlow 2</em> by Sebastian Raschka and Vahid Mirjalili</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>More ways to \"Dive into Machine Learning\"</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers\">Machine Learning for Software Engineers, by Nam Vu</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">25.6k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":25556,\"repo\":\"ZuzooVn/machine-learning-for-software-engineers\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->. In their words, it's a \"top-down and results-first approach designed for software engineers.\" Definitely bookmark and use it, as well - it can answer lots of questions and connect you with great resources.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:59:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"davidsonfellipe/awesome-wpo","categoryHTML":"<h2>CDN</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudfront/\">Amazon CloudFront</a> - A content delivery network by Amazon that integrates nicely with other Amazon services or can be used standalone.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-11-21T05:44:56.000Z"}]}},"pageContext":{"type":"day","from":1637452800000,"to":1637539199999,"previousId":"2021-11-22","nextId":"2021-11-20","nextName":"Nov 20th, 2021","previousName":"Nov 22nd, 2021"}},"staticQueryHashes":["228695001","2744905544","2828988102"]}